  "id": "applied-sport-psychology",
  "term": "applied sport psychology",
  "definition": "Applied sport psychology is the practical use of psychological ideas and consultation in sport to help athletes improve how they prepare and perform. In this source, it is described as a field that has mainly emphasized competition readiness and performance, while giving less attention to the psychology of practice and the self-regulation of training.",
