      "reasons": [
        "The definition’s first sentence (“the practical use of psychological ideas and consultation in sport”) is not explicitly stated in the packet as the definition of applied sport psychology; the packet discusses sport psychology consultants and applied research, but does not define the term in that exact way.",
        "The second sentence’s claim about “less attention to the psychology of practice and the self-regulation of training” is only partially supported: the packet argues that the “psychology of sport practice” / “psychology of practice” is underappreciated or under-considered, and it focuses on self-regulated sport practice via the SRSP, but it does not clearly phrase this as “self-regulation of training” more generally."
